2026-11-06T02:59:51.3572567Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3580629Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581020Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581254Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581364Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581487Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581614Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581735Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3581964Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3582082Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3582147Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3582325Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3582495Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3582651Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3583014Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T02:59:51.3583133Z 
